 "intro": "Tapae, the pass leading to the heart of Dacia (in modern Romania), 88 AD. Two years ago the Dacian king Decebalus destroyed a Roman army. You are Tettius Julianus, sent by the Emperor Domitian.",
 "debrief": "In Cassius Dio’s account, Julianus had every soldier write his name and his centurion’s on his shield, so bravery would be noticed. He beat the Dacians at Tapae; their general Vezinas escaped by lying among the dead. Decebalus is said to have cut down trees and dressed them in armour to make the Romans halt. Domitian, at war elsewhere, made peace, making Decebalus a client king. The other choices are what-ifs.",
